From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:02:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(mcp-registry): allow * patterns in the tool allowlist

A registry service lists the upstream tools it allows by exact name, so
the registry file has to be regenerated and the server restarted whenever
the service adds a tool. For services with many tools (a search endpoint
per index, generated tool sets) that list is long and goes stale.

An entry in `tools` may now hold `*`, standing for any run of characters:
`search_*`, `*_read`, `get_*_by_id`, and `"*"` alone for every tool. The
match is literal, case-sensitive and anchored at both ends; no regular
expression is built from the file. Exact names behave as before.

Patterns are not expanded when tools are listed. Every place that checked
membership in the list (tool discovery, the gateway listing and each call
on the gateway and legacy session routes) asks the service instead, so
the allowlist is enforced on the server for every call and a tool that
appears upstream later is admitted or refused by its name. `"*"` must be
the only entry and is logged at startup; `**`, `?` and `[...]` in a
pattern fail validation. The registry has no deny list and none is
added: user allowlists, an agent's own tool list and policies keep
narrowing on top, and a policy deny still wins.

A server without this change reads a pattern as an exact name that
matches nothing, so patterns are replaced with names before a rollback;
the registry README says so.

Not upstream yet: not proposed, and there is no contribution branch for
it. Upstream's design describes the exact allowlist as the
administrator's review step (designs/MCP_REGISTRY_GATEWAY.md), and no
open issue or pull request asks for patterns.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
